---
title: How to Use My Tasks
description: >-
  See your tasks from every project in one place, filter and group them by
  client, program or category, and choose which columns to show.
sidebar:
  order: 18
---
**My Tasks gathers the tasks assigned to you from every project into one list. Use it to plan your day, see which client or program each task belongs to, and open any task without going project by project.**

You find it in the sidebar as **My Task**. The page header shows how many tasks are open, how many are overdue or due today, how many projects they span, and the time you logged this week.

### **Pick What You See**

Use the tabs under the title to narrow the list by date:

- **All open**
- **Today**
- **Next 7 days**
- **Overdue**
- **No due date**
- **Completed**

Each tab shows how many tasks it holds. Use the search box to find a task by its title, its key or its project.

Switch between four views with the buttons next to the search box:

- **List** shows one row per task, with columns.
- **Board** shows cards in columns by the way you group.
- **Calendar** puts tasks on the days they are due.
- **Timeline** draws each task as a bar across the week. Use the arrows and **Today** to move between weeks.

### **Filter the List**

Click **Filter** to narrow the list. The filters you set show as chips under the toolbar, and **Clear** removes them all.

- **Assignee.** **Assigned to me**, **Created by me**, or **Both**.
- **Team member.** See another person's tasks. Only Administrators and Managers see this filter, and you still only see tasks in projects you can open.
- **Client.** Only tasks in projects that belong to that client.
- **Program.** Only tasks in projects that belong to a [program](/project-management/how-to-use-programs-and-categories/).
- **Category.** Only tasks in projects that have a [category](/project-management/how-to-use-programs-and-categories/).
- **Status**, **Priority**, **Type** and **Project.** Pick one or several.

Click **Apply** to use your choices. Filters are saved in the page address, so you can bookmark or share a filtered list.

### **Group and Sort**

Click **Group** to choose how tasks are grouped:

- **Due date**
- **Project**
- **Program**
- **Category**
- **Status**
- **Priority**
- **Type**
- **Label**
- **No grouping**

When you group by **Project**, the client or company is shown next to the project's name, so two projects with the same name for different customers are easy to tell apart.

When you group by **Program** or **Category**, a task whose project has no program or category goes under **No program** or **No category** at the end. A project with several categories appears under each of them.

Use the sort button to order tasks by **Due date**, **Priority**, **Last updated**, **Created**, **Title** or **Project**, ascending or descending.

### **Choose Your Columns**

Click the **...** menu at the right of the toolbar to open the display options.

- **Density.** **Comfortable** or **Compact** rows.
- **Show in list.** Tick the columns you want: **Project**, **Client**, **Program**, **Category**, **Status**, **Priority**, **Due date**, **Assignees**, **Time & timer**, **Labels** and **Subtasks & activity**.

The **Client** column is on by default. It shows the company when the project has one, and otherwise the client's name. Hover over it to see every client and company on the project. **Program** and **Category** are off by default, so turn them on when you need them.

When many columns are on, the list scrolls sideways so task titles stay readable. Your choices are saved in your browser.

### **Good to Know**

- A project can [hide its task keys](/project-management/how-to-manage-project-in-taskip/#show-or-hide-the-task-prefix). Its tasks then show no key such as TTM-5 anywhere, including here.
- Names follow your workspace's [terminology](/settings/client-portal-settings/). If you renamed Project to Job, the list says **Job**.
- Clients never see this page.
